                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1317-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_hc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Hypercardioid" title="Hypercardioid" ></span>Audio-Technica ATM610a</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Hypercardioid Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>ATM610a is an updated version of Audio-Technica&#8217;s ATM610. Both are hypercardioid stage vocal microphones made with Neodymium magnets. </p><p>The ATM610a features an upgraded capsule shockmount and a multi-stage windscreen.</p><p>The differences between the ATM610 and ATM610a include:</p><ul><li>The 610a has an improved internal shockmount, which reduces handling noise</li><li>The 610a is 10g lighter</li><li>The 610a has 3dB better rejection at 180&deg; (although the polar patterns are otherwise nearly identical).</li><li>The frequency response differs slightly; the 610a is flat from 100&ndash;300Hz, whereas the ATM610 had a small boost in this region.</li></ul><p>A variation on ATM610a, the ATM610a/S features a lockable MagnaLock on/off switch design providing silent on/off operation.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Audio-Technica/ATM610a">Audio-Technica ATM610a</a> is also known as: ATM-610A, ATM-610a/S, ATM-610.</p><p>The mic was released in 2012.</p>
